Installing OpenABL from Android (needs root)

1. Copy this rocknix_abl folder from the SD card to the top level of Android's
   internal storage.
2. As root, run backup_abl.sh from that folder. It saves your current
   bootloader, so you can always go back to it.
3. Then, as root, run flash_abl.sh to install OpenABL.
4. Turn the handheld off. Hold Volume Down while turning it on to open the
   OpenABL menu. Volume Up and Down move, Power selects.
5. Set these three:
     Boot mode    -> Linux
     Boot source  -> SD card (or Auto)
     Device model -> your handheld (for example Retroid Pocket 6)
   Don't skip Device model. Without one, OpenABL won't start Steamling and
   drops you straight back into this menu.
6. Pick Start.
